# SaaS-shape local dev: Clerk auth, Voyage embeddings. Used by `make dev` here
# and by the workspace's `make dev` / `make saas-dev`.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Postgres and Qdrant come from docker-compose.dev.yml (`make dev-db-up`).
# The workspace `make saas-dev` overrides DATABASE_URL, QDRANT_COLLECTION,
# STORAGE_BACKEND and PORT with its own throwaway stack, so those lines only
# matter for `make dev`.
#
# Format: the Makefile feeds this file through `grep | xargs`, so use
# KEY=value lines and full-line comments only. No quotes, no spaces in values,
# no comments after a value. Leave an optional key commented out rather than
# empty: an empty value is still "set".

# --- Stores (docker-compose.dev.yml) ----------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://engram:engram@localhost:5433/engram_dev
QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6334
QDRANT_COLLECTION=engram_dev
# Binary quantization needs an AVX2 CPU; without it Qdrant dies with SIGILL.
# QDRANT_BINARY_QUANTIZATION=false
STORAGE_BACKEND=database

# --- App --------------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=4000
KEY_PROVIDER=local
# Required. Generate once with `openssl rand -base64 32`.
ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY=

# --- Auth: your own Clerk development instance ------------------------------
# From the API keys page of a Clerk dev instance you control. frontend/.env.local
# needs the same publishable key as VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# (see frontend/.env.local.example).
AUTH_PROVIDER=clerk
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your-key
CLERK_ISSUER=https://your-instance.clerk.accounts.dev
CLERK_JWKS_URL=https://your-instance.clerk.accounts.dev/.well-known/jwks.json
# Optional: duplicate-signup revocation and Clerk webhooks.
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your-key
# CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your-secret

# --- Embeddings: pick ONE ---------------------------------------------------
# Option A: Voyage AI with your own key (SaaS shape).
EMBED_BACKEND=voyage
VOYAGE_API_KEY=pa-your-key
EMBED_MODEL=voyage-4-large
EMBED_DIMS=1024
DOC_EMBED_MODEL=voyage-4-large
QUERY_EMBED_MODEL=voyage-4-lite

# Option B: Ollama, no API key (comment out Option A). Run
# `ollama pull mxbai-embed-large` on any host you can reach.
# EMBED_BACKEND=ollama
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# EMBED_MODEL=mxbai-embed-large
# EMBED_DIMS=1024

# --- Optional: billing (Paddle sandbox) and email (Resend) ------------------
# Billing stays off until PADDLE_API_KEY is set.
# PADDLE_ENV=sandbox
# PADDLE_API_KEY=your-sandbox-key
# PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=your-client-token
# PADDLE_NOTIFICATION_SECRET=your-secret
# Email is a no-op until RESEND_API_KEY is set.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_your-key
# EMAIL_FROM=you@example.com
